Id: lin025w
Severity: WARN
Category: kernel
Check: check_sysctl
Fix: Set kernel.unprivileged_bpf_disabled=1 in /etc/sysctl.d.
References: sysctl.d(5); Linux kernel sysctl documentation
Controls: CIS 4.1, 10.5; NIST CM-6, SI-16; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

kernel.unprivileged_bpf_disabled is 0, so unprivileged users may load
BPF programs into the kernel. The BPF verifier has been the source of
several privilege escalations. 1 disables it until reboot, 2 until the
next change:
  # sysctl -w kernel.unprivileged_bpf_disabled=1
